+Seventh request: a one-line cellular-automaton rule spec ("domino CA. 4
+upright orientations... falling transitions to a single fallen state...")
+with no reference link and, notably, genuine ambiguity in the transition
+condition itself (several self-consistent readings of "not orthogonal &
+not pushing in opposite directions" produce different automata). Consistent
+with the established pattern of calling out mathematically-valid shortcuts
+rather than silently picking one: this build picked one reading, worked it
+through by hand to confirm it was coherent (straight hits topple, diagonal/
+orthogonal/opposite hits don't), and stated the interpretation explicitly
+on-page and in NOTE.txt/BRIEF.md rather than presenting it as the only
+possible reading. Untested against a reaction yet, but the expectation this
+profile already tracks — flag the ambiguity before being asked — applied
+here to a CA rule rather than a polynomial family.
